{"type": "FeatureCollection", "features": [{"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Marquette, Houghton and Ontonagon Railroad", "line": "Marquette, Houghton and Ontonagon: Marquette \u2013 Ishpeming", "id": "mho-marquette-negaunee-ishpeming", "color": "#4A4E69", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 25, "speed_source": "estimated: 1850s-80s iron-range industrial line; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1857, "end": 1890, "headway_min": 480, "note": "Chartered 1852 by Herman Ely and family as the Iron Mountain Railroad - the first common-carrier railroad in Michigan's Upper Peninsula - to move iron ore from the Marquette Range mines (Negaunee, Ishpeming) to a shipping dock at Marquette; completed August 1857. Renamed several times (Bay de Noquet & Marquette, then Marquette & Ontonagon), consolidating with the Houghton & Ontonagon in 1872 as the Marquette, Houghton and Ontonagon Railroad. Frequency estimated, unsourced.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duluth"]}]}, "geometry": {"type": "LineString", "coordinates": [[-87.6305899, 46.4481521], [-87.611803, 46.499102], [-87.667636, 46.488547]]}}, {"type": "Feature", "properties": {"company": "Duluth, South Shore and Atlantic Railway", "line": "Duluth, South Shore and Atlantic: Sault Ste. Marie \u2013 Duluth", "id": "dssa-saultstemarie-marquette-duluth", "color": "#4A4E69", "mode": "intercity_rail", "avg_speed_kmh": 45, "speed_source": "estimated: typical Lake Superior-shore mainline service of the era; unsourced", "segments": [{"start": 1890, "end": 1958, "headway_min": 360, "note": "The DSS&A was organized in 1890 to buy up and unify the Marquette, Houghton and Ontonagon and other predecessor lines (having leased the MH&O since Feb 15, 1887), assembling a through route along the Lake Superior shore from Sault Ste. Marie and St. Ignace through Marquette to Superior, WI and Duluth, MN. All DSS&A passenger service ended in January 1958, following the 1957 opening of the Mackinac Bridge which shifted Upper Peninsula travel to cars; the UP has had no intercity passenger rail since, and was never part of the Amtrak system. Merged into the Soo Line in 1961. Frequency estimated, unsourced. Route follows the real DSS&A alignment via Newberry/Soo Junction (the Sault Ste. Marie branch left the main line here, reached 1887), Seney, Shingleton, Marquette, Michigamme, Nestoria (Keweenaw branch junction), Ontonagon, Wakefield, Ironwood, Hurley/Mellen WI, and Ashland before reaching Superior and Duluth.", "sources": ["NOT SOURCED AT SEGMENT LEVEL: the references below cover this line, but nothing has been checked specifically against this segment's start year, end year or service. Treat the dates and the headway as unverified. Supporting references for the line:", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duluth"]}], "geometry_repairs": [{"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-84.3476583, 46.4976734], "to": [-85.5098868, 46.3559523], "chord_mi": 56.16, "traced_mi": 64.65, "snap_m": [742, 89], "bridged_mi": 1.11, "osm_lines": ["Soo/Strong Trail [abandoned] (28.19 mi)", "(abandoned) [abandoned] (18.13 mi)", "Newberry Subdivision (11.84 mi)", "DSS&A [abandoned] (3.65 mi)", "Manistique Subdivision (1.29 mi)", "(?) (1.11 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rail graph, 8.4 km corridor, Dijkstra, simplified to 3.0 m; 1.11 mi bridged across gaps in OSM"}, {"date": "2026-08-29", "from": [-90.1836208, 46.449879], "to": [-90.6606627, 46.3257496], "chord_mi": 24.26, "traced_mi": 26.51, "snap_m": [99, 62], "bridged_mi": 0.0, "osm_lines": ["(abandoned) [abandoned] (25.9 mi)", "(disused) [disused] (0.29 mi)", "Iron Horse Trail [abandoned] (0.24 mi)", "Wisconsin Central Railroad [disused] (0.05 mi)", "Abandoned Railroad [abandoned] (0.03 mi)"], "method": "Overpass rai